{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:5b7f5a0f628062b7","name":"The Exchange","source":{"id":"source:reference-5b7f5a0f628062b7","title":"The Exchange","revision":22630,"timestamp":"2024-09-05T23:53:20Z","sha256":"71398bd76df90249f20d3061af208d1b65c551f5b78bc02eae203b081f78fe9b","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=22630","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=The%20Exchange&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-5b7f5a0f628062b7","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Exchange is one of the largest criminal networks in the galaxy. Though their operations thrive on ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Outer Rim"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Outer_Rim?action=edit&redlink=1"},"- outside Republic control and law enforcement- elements of their schemes and organization can be found throughout the galaxy. The organization is said to be run by an entity or individual known as ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Compeer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Compeer?action=edit&redlink=1"},", but the person's location and identity remain mysterious, even to those high up in Exchange leadership.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["On each planet where The Exchange has significant influence, a powerful crime lord oversees all Exchange operations. Each of these crime lords comes to power through the approval of and election by the other Exchange leaders. Though nominally allies, they compete for power, influence, and control. As masters of their respective planets, they were responsible for their operations' successes and failures. Notable leaders include ",{"tag":"a","children":["Davik Kang"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Davik_Kang?action=edit&redlink=1"}," of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Taris"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Taris","referenceId":"reference:6c77edc098cd2a27"},"- who is killed when ",{"tag":"a","children":["Revan"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Revan","referenceId":"reference:9199cff8278e357a"}," and others steal his ship, ",{"tag":"a","children":["The ",{"tag":"i","children":["Ebon Hawk"]}],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Ebon_Hawk","referenceId":"reference:2c6a06fa640aebe7"}," - and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Goto"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Goto"},", alias of the Droid ",{"tag":"a","children":["G0-T0"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/G0-T0","referenceId":"reference:0da0c54e9c222f3c"},", who controls a major smuggling operation at ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nar Shaddaa"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nar_Shaddaa","referenceId":"reference:69680e00e40913c9"}," years later.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Exchange can be found on nearly all developed planets. Anyone with the right reputation, or determination, can eventually make contact with the organization. In fact, those who display particular aptitude in an area The Exchange wishes to exploit might attract overtures, threats, or both, depending on the response. Smugglers are always needed, but bounty hunters, mercenaries, slave traders, and infiltrators are also recruited.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Exchange has a peculiar hierarchy, which few have managed to uncover. The Exchange maintains organized cells on worlds of interest, and each of those planetary cells is led by a single boss who rules over Exchange interests on that world. The bosses report to sector chiefs who have no cells of their own (though they might have a smaller support staff) and operate under secret identities, leading normal lives. Even the bosses do not know who the chiefs are in real life, as most communications are done over secret, secure communications channels. The chiefs report to the head of The Exchange, who is themselves a sector chief, so if a single sector chief's cover is compromised, the organization merely appears to be ruled by a council of sector chiefs.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Exchange Units"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Nonheroic Units"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["NAME\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["CHALLENGE LEVEL\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["SOURCE\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Kath Hound"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Kath_Hound","referenceId":"reference:b6155e97a22e5692"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["CL 3\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Kath Hound Pack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Kath_Hound_Pack","referenceId":"reference:3c7906b9f7a3153b"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["CL 5\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Threats of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Threats_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["HK-50 Assassin Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/HK-50_Assassin_Droid","referenceId":"reference:a2066fc1bd136acf"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["CL 12\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Heroic Units"]},"\n"